  "body": "The selected R480 supplier cannot defer any of its 402 final helper climbs\nthrough its unchanged physical FULL-frame cleanup while keeping canonical\ndata outputs and arbitrary source-independent helper boundary types.\nThe proof covers dense helper mixing, arbitrary fiber dimensions and all\nbatch lengths and finite recursive depths. Exact inverse-source witnesses\ngive the obstruction; the optimum is zero omitted climbs.\n\nReview files: [Proof and scope](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/3bceac90599a02a96e9b744736b3feeb00171504/research/r480-source-independent-cleanup/README.md) \u00b7 [Evidence](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/3bceac90599a02a96e9b744736b3feeb00171504/research/r480-source-independent-cleanup/CERTIFICATE.json) \u00b7 [Source pins and credit](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/3bceac90599a02a96e9b744736b3feeb00171504/research/r480-source-independent-cleanup/SOURCES.json).\n\nThe package also classifies the larger backward target-covariance interface:\n19 free operator components on 22 helpers. It checks their native ranks and\nmandatory output repairs. For each paired rank-one tail, a uniform inequality\nexcludes a moment saving with any host of rank at most eight, even with free\nscalar adapters and perfect fusion. Changed native cleanup, source-history\nprotocols, joint encodings and changed owners remain open.\n\nThe selected local and global profiles are unchanged, so the conditional\nkappa remains 0.001672660197076918. This is a scoped mathematical obstruction,\nnot a new exponent or a new native construction.\n\nValidation: the registered Python 3.12 replay passes. It checks both complete\n712-coordinate scalar maps, all 402 helper witnesses, all 78 isolated\nnonfinal helpers, identical directional climb events, two independent exact\ncovariance classifications, native frames, target projectors, owner ranks,\nand eight boundary controls. Direct optimized replays also passed on\nPython 3.9.6 and 3.14.7. A read-only relocated fixture passed, and altered\nsource bytes and certificate coefficients were rejected. No full selected\ncold replay, new hosted stream, or hosted CI run is claimed.\n\nReproduce from the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/r480-source-independent-cleanup\n```\n\nBase: [bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f). Audited supplier source:\n[0fc329d0bec93ca7cd288eaea1295172e8789810](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/0fc329d0bec93ca7cd288eaea1295172e8789810). The new package contains the proof,\nexact certificate, immutable source pins, original task card, and replay\nmanifest. No selected record, frozen input or upstream file changes.\n\nPrepared by Ali Romman (@aliromman) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in algebra,\nimplementation, proof review, verification and writing. Credit the retained\n[PR #1094](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1094), [PR #1042](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1042) supplier lineage; Sagar Thakrar (@thakrarsagar)'s [PR #1012](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1012) and [PR #1227](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1227); Ross Richardson (@RossRichardson)'s [PR #1287](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1287); @Scratch-net's [PR #1198](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1198); and the reader-contract and native\nframe predecessors listed in the package. New work is Apache-2.0.\n",
